===Etymology 1===
Earlier spelling {{m|en|Marocco}}, from {{der|en|pt|Marrocos}} and/or {{der|en|es|Marruecos}}, from {{der|en|ar|مُرَّاكُش}}, from {{der|en|ber}} {{m|zgh|[[ⴰⵎⵓⵔ]] [[ⵏ]] [[ⴰⴽⵓⵛ]]|lit=Land of God}}. The word originally referred to the capital city of {{m|en|Marrakech}} (founded late 11th c.), but came to be used as a [[pars pro toto]] for the westernmost region of the Islamic world. Compare older {{cog|ar|مُرَّاكُش}} (now {{m|ar|اَلْمَغْرِب}}), {{cog|fa|مراکش|tr=marâkeš}}, {{cog|ML.|Marrochium}}. {{cog|tr|-}} refers to the country as {{m|tr|Fas}} from {{m|en|Fez}}, another former capital. {{doublet|en|Marrakech}}.

